"""Text report from completed cost-layer price rows, without rerunning."""
import csv,json,hashlib
from decimal import Decimal as D
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;r=list(csv.DictReader((p/'prices_33_by_limit.csv').open()));s=json.loads((p/'summary.json').read_text());assert len(r)==132
manifest=p/'VM_KERNEL_POSITION_MANIFEST.txt';lines=manifest.read_text().splitlines();assert len(lines)==480
low=[x for x in r if x['price_model_units'] and D(x['price_model_units'])<20]
lines=['# PR427 price-only flight-limit sensitivity','','**TEST_ONLY / NON-CANON. No economic campaign run.** 90-body/20-sponsor world, 2026–2226 campaign context. This prices only the 33 previously unstarted bodies, with the held-2026 departure rule.','','Authored scenario: `scenario.json`; SHA-256 `'+s['scenario_sha256']+'`. Limits: 1,400 / 3,000 / 5,000 / 8,000 days.','Clean input prices SHA-256: `'+s['clean_price_sha256']+'`.','Fixed-cost floor: 0.7 model units; **fail on violation, never clamp**. All 42 priced rows passed.','','**Important coverage distinction:** The 1,400-day rows reuse the accepted complete-cost-layer 2026 quotes, rather than recomputing them. The 3,000-day rows are new cost-layer calculations where existing validated position tables cover the full requested flight window. A `NO DATA` row means the **existing position table** does not cover the listed required date, not that no suitable kernel exists anywhere on the VM. No kernel-derived tables were created in this job. Thus 5,000/8,000-day prices remain unresolved, not economically ruled out.','','## Prices and missing data','','| Body | Limit days | Price (model units) | Flight days | Braking km/s | Status / exact missing position |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for x in r:
 price=x['price_model_units'] or '—';days=x['flight_days'] or '—';brake=x['arrival_braking_km_s'] or '—';reason=f"NO DATA: {x['missing_position_body']} {x['missing_position_date']}" if x['status']=='NO DATA' else x['status'];lines.append(f"| {x['body']} | {x['limit_days']} | {price} | {days} | {brake} | {reason} |")
lines+=['','## Below 20 model units','','| Body | First limit priced below 20 | Price (model units) |','|---|---:|---:|']
for x in low:lines.append(f"| {x['body']} | {x['limit_days']} | {x['price_model_units']} |")
lines+=['','The first six Uranus/Neptune moon rows to cross below 20 are at 3,000 days. CHIRON was already below 20 at 1,400 days. No conclusion is possible for bodies with NO DATA at longer limits.','','## Position provenance and independent checks','','- No new position tables were built. Therefore no new-table independent comparison was performed: **NOT APPLICABLE**, not a fresh PASS.','- The 3,000-day pricing uses the existing 2035 numeric tables for EARTH and relevant outer planets. Their existing manifest reports 14,425 validation and epoch-roundtrip samples per planet; source SHA-256 and table SHA-256 were checked before lookup.','- Existing recovered 34-body tables end 2031-10-31; existing numeric nine-planet tables end 2035-12-31. The 5,000-day requirement from 2026-02-15 reaches 2039-10-25; 8,000 reaches 2048-01-11.','- A separate text-only asset inventory covers 477 kernel/position-table files under `/home/ubuntu/loom_solar_assets` and `/home/ubuntu/LOOM-output`. File paths, byte sizes, and SHA-256 are recorded in `VM_KERNEL_POSITION_MANIFEST.txt`. No binary assets are committed.','- Manifest SHA-256: `'+hashlib.sha256(manifest.read_bytes()).hexdigest()+'`.','','## Controls','','- Route 1 replay control: **PASS** `'+s['route1_hash']+'`.','- Floor: **PASS** for all priced rows.','- Retry rules: unchanged; no campaign executed.','- Database SHA-256 before and after: `e21304e687e63e264edb44f36ff7c68fa3f119307315bce49008711547fa7cde`.','- No downloads, installations, or edits to pre-existing files.','']
(p/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));print('REPORT',len(r),'low',[(x['body'],x['limit_days']) for x in low],flush=True)
